<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>6.7.0: Lesson Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01696</md:content-id>
    <md:title>6.7.0: Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>955f270c-b141-4ea7-8e7f-6d7df69ae636</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you will review each strategy learned throughout this unit to assess the best strategy to factor polynomials. You will be presented with different polynomials, and, without additional context, you will find the fully factored form of each.</para>
<para id="para-00002">When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list id="list-00001">
  <item>Recognize and use the appropriate method to factor a polynomial completely.</item>
</list>
<para id="para-00003">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list id="list-00002">
  <item>6.7.1: Factoring Strategies for Polynomials</item>
  <item>6.7.2: Reviewing General Strategies to Factor a Polynomial<list id="list-00003">
    <item>6.7.2: Self Check</item>
    <item>6.7.2: Additional Resources</item>
  </list></item>
  
  <item>6.7.3: Implementing General Strategies for Factoring <list id="list-00004">
    <item>6.7.3: Self Check</item>
    <item>6.7.3: Additional Resources</item>
  </list></item>
 
  <item>6.7.4: Is the Polynomial Completely Factored?</item>
</list>
<para id="para-00004">After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list id="list-00005">
  <item>6.7.5: Practice</item>
  <item>6.7.6: Lesson Summary</item>
</list></section>
</content>
</document>